From 0860808a94bd48f9a2551761af686b02b921493f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 4evy <git@evy.pink>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0300
Subject: redate: align the revision picker with native TUIs

Use a borderless title/main/status layout with stable checked markers and a full-row focus highlight so graph glyphs only describe topology. Keep the focused revision timestamp in the title bar, make key hints responsive, and add select-all, boundary navigation, anchored Shift range selection, and the standard c-to-confirm binding.

Use jj's standard prompt for timestamps instead of a bespoke raw-mode line editor. Accept exact and relative local-time expressions, add --timestamp for non-interactive use, preserve explicit offsets, and cover the interaction and responsive layouts with tests.

